  "source_review": [
    "The fixed26-label unchanged RAM program resets scratch registers, scans rows/selected columns, reads source entries and writes dense output. Cyclic indices use actual increment/equality/reset; division/remainder occur only in the mathematical memory specification. Prefix/cyclic paths are padded to the same11-step per-entry proof.",
    "Valid requires positive tied count, bounded start/take and valid prefix. The cyclic block need fit the source matrix only when take>0; this correctly admits pure prefix take0/above=rows and empty cases. width\u2264rows and every used source address lies in the actual square input block are separately proved.",
    "Under exactly the original DisjointBlocks condition for full square source and dense output, every actual legal trace gathers the old source cells and preserves all memory outside output. Initial memory is proved equal to old memory by frameGatherMemory_zero; no gathered matrix is supplied as program data.",
    "Standalone traces halt at rows*(11*width+7)+5 with the actual charged-cost bound. Every valid caller embedding and arbitrary call offset returns running at mapped local halt25 before executing it, with actual cells, outside-memory preservation and prefix-plus rows*(11*width+7)+4 cost.",
    "Actual generic matrix readback is identified with the explicit cyclic tie frame (using the exact rank cast) and literal U-prefix frame. Independent composed consumer examples check these two identifications directly against arbitrary legal caller traces."
  ],
